{"parentUuid":"0bc1bfd9-b98c-4b56-a6f8-0f504bc30aa6","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"260b5336-3a47-4997-b0ce-d48901003928","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-fluttering-newell","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_011otoDdUE99ndCXW3HaNmqU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Xyv2YDbchDqpod4MGQoqXT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-streaming-api.md","content":"# Apache Flink Streaming API (1.18.x)\n\n## Overview\nApache Flink is a distributed stream processing framework. This skill covers the DataStream API for building streaming jobs.\n\n## Setup\n- Flink 1.18.0 with Java 11\n- Dependencies: `flink-streaming-java`, `flink-java`, `flink-clients`\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### StreamExecutionEnvironment\n```java\nStreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();\n```\n\n### Reading from files (including gzipped)\n```java\n// Flink can read .gz files natively\nDataStream<String> lines = env.readTextFile(\"/path/to/file.csv.gz\");\n```\n\n### DataStream Transformations\n```java\n// Map: transform each element\nDataStream<MyType> mapped = lines.map(line -> parse(line));\n\n// Filter\nDataStream<MyType> filtered = mapped.filter(e -> e.type == 0);\n\n// KeyBy: partition by key for grouped processing\nKeyedStream<MyType, Long> keyed = filtered.keyBy(e -> e.jobId);\n\n// Reduce: aggregate elements per key\nDataStream<MyType> reduced = keyed.reduce((a, b) -> combine(a, b));\n```\n\n### Window Operations\n```java\n// Event time session windows with gap\nkeyed\n  .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n  .process(new ProcessWindowFunction<>() {\n      @Override\n      public void process(Long key, Context ctx,\n              Iterable<TaskEvent> elements, Collector<Tuple2<Long,Long>> out) {\n          long count = 0;\n          for (TaskEvent e : elements) count++;\n          out.collect(new Tuple2<>(key, count));\n      }\n  });\n```\n\n### Event Time & Watermarks\n```java\n// Assign timestamps and watermarks for event-time processing\nDataStream<MyEvent> withTimestamps = stream\n    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n        WatermarkStrategy.<MyEvent>forMonotonousTimestamps()\n            .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.timestamp / 1000) // convert micros to millis\n    );\n```\n\n### Writing Output\n```java\n// Write to text file\nresult.writeAsText(\"/path/to/output\", FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE)\n      .setParallelism(1);\n```\n\n### Connecting Streams\n```java\n// Connect two streams for co-processing\nDataStream<A> streamA = ...;\nDataStream<B> streamB = ...;\nConnectedStreams<A, B> connected = streamA.connect(streamB);\nDataStream<Result> result = connected.keyBy(a -> a.key, b -> b.key)\n    .process(new CoProcessFunction<>() { ... });\n```\n\n### Tuple Types\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.tuple.Tuple2;\nTuple2<Long, Long> t = new Tuple2<>(jobId, count);\n// Output format: (jobId,count)\n```\n\n## Event Time Processing Notes\n- Flink event time is in **milliseconds**\n- Google cluster data timestamps are in **microseconds**\n- Must convert: `eventTimeMicros / 1000` for Flink timestamps\n- Use `WatermarkStrategy.forMonotonousTimestamps()` when data is sorted by time\n- Use `WatermarkStrategy.forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration)` for out-of-order data\n\n## Session Windows\nSession windows group elements that arrive within a specified gap of each other.\n- `EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10))` creates sessions with 10-minute gap\n- Elements within 10 minutes of each other are in the same session\n- Session closes when no new elements arrive for 10 minutes\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107,"cache_read_input_tokens":48740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":107,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtEhLArbDwBA1wwYMW3z","type":"assistant","uuid":"252c618e-6fe0-4297-bc45-60c6e8e8824b","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:29:54.409Z"}
{"parentUuid":"252c618e-6fe0-4297-bc45-60c6e8e8824b","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"260b5336-3a47-4997-b0ce-d48901003928","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-fluttering-newell","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_011otoDdUE99ndCXW3HaNmqU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01WB1ZqdcqEhPhZK8WbaHhHw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/google-cluster-data-schema.md","content":"# Google Cluster Data 2011-2 Schema\n\n## Overview\nThe Google cluster-usage traces dataset (clusterdata-2011-2) represents 29 days of Borg cell information from May 2011. All timestamps are in **microseconds**.\n\n## Task Events Table\nCSV with 13 fields (0-indexed):\n\n| Index | Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | timestamp | long | Event time in microseconds |\n| 1 | missing_info | string | Info about missing data (can be empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | task_index | int | Task index within the job |\n| 4 | machine_id | long | Machine the task runs on (can be empty) |\n| 5 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 6 | user | string | Hashed user name |\n| 7 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class (0-3) |\n| 8 | priority | int | Priority level (0-11) |\n| 9 | cpu_request | double | CPU resource request |\n| 10 | memory_request | double | Memory resource request |\n| 11 | disk_request | double | Disk resource request |\n| 12 | different_machines_restriction | int | Machine constraint |\n\n## Job Events Table\nCSV with 8 fields (0-indexed):\n\n| Index | Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | timestamp | long | Event time in microseconds |\n| 1 | missing_info | string | Info about missing data (can be empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 4 | user | string | Hashed user name |\n| 5 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class |\n| 6 | job_name | string | Hashed job name |\n| 7 | logical_job_name | string | Hashed logical job name |\n\n## Event Types (shared for both job and task events)\n| Value | Name | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | SUBMIT | Job/task submitted |\n| 1 | SCHEDULE | Job/task scheduled on machine |\n| 2 | EVICT | Task evicted from machine |\n| 3 | FAIL | Task/job failed |\n| 4 | FINISH | Task/job finished normally |\n| 5 | KILL | Task/job killed |\n| 6 | LOST | Task lost (communication failure) |\n| 7 | UPDATE_PENDING | Task resource request updated while pending |\n| 8 | UPDATE_RUNNING | Task resource request updated while running |\n\n## Notes\n- Fields can be empty (e.g., machine_id for SUBMIT events)\n- Timestamps start at ~600 seconds (= 600,000,000 microseconds)\n- Data files are gzipped CSV with no header row\n- Job IDs are shared between task_events and job_events tables\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107,"cache_read_input_tokens":48740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":107,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtEhLArbDwBA1wwYMW3z","type":"assistant","uuid":"bf60f992-a50b-42ec-b198-1872f171077e","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:30:04.849Z"}
{"parentUuid":"bf60f992-a50b-42ec-b198-1872f171077e","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"260b5336-3a47-4997-b0ce-d48901003928","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-fluttering-newell","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_011otoDdUE99ndCXW3HaNmqU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01D9dcrKik5qFydmUr9Zy8Se","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-session-window-pattern.md","content":"# Flink Session Window Pattern for Stage Detection\n\n## Problem Pattern\nIdentify \"stages\" of activity for a keyed entity based on event-time gaps. A stage ends when there's a period of inactivity exceeding a threshold.\n\n## Solution: Event-Time Session Windows\n\n### Approach\n1. Parse input events, extract timestamp and key\n2. Assign event-time timestamps and watermarks\n3. Filter to relevant events (e.g., SUBMIT events only)\n4. Key by the grouping field (e.g., job_id)\n5. Apply session window with the inactivity gap\n6. Count elements per window to get stage sizes\n7. Take the maximum stage size per key\n\n### Implementation Pattern\n\n```java\n// Step 1-2: Parse and assign timestamps\nDataStream<TaskEvent> taskEvents = env.readTextFile(inputPath)\n    .map(line -> TaskEvent.parse(line))\n    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n        WatermarkStrategy.<TaskEvent>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ZERO)\n            .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.timestamp / 1000)\n    );\n\n// Step 3-4: Filter SUBMIT events and key by job\nDataStream<TaskEvent> submits = taskEvents.filter(e -> e.eventType == 0);\nKeyedStream<TaskEvent, Long> keyed = submits.keyBy(e -> e.jobId);\n\n// Step 5-6: Session window + count\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> stageCounts = keyed\n    .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .apply(new WindowFunction<TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Long>, Long, TimeWindow>() {\n        @Override\n        public void apply(Long jobId, TimeWindow window,\n                Iterable<TaskEvent> input, Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) {\n            long count = 0;\n            for (TaskEvent e : input) count++;\n            out.collect(new Tuple2<>(jobId, count));\n        }\n    });\n\n// Step 7: Find max stage per job\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> maxStagePerJob = stageCounts\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0)\n    .reduce((a, b) -> a.f1 >= b.f1 ? a : b);\n```\n\n### Key Considerations\n- **Timestamp conversion**: Google cluster data uses microseconds, Flink uses milliseconds\n- **Watermark strategy**: Use monotonous timestamps if data is sorted, bounded out-of-orderness otherwise\n- **Parallelism**: Set output sink to parallelism 1 to get single output file\n- **Session gap**: 10 minutes = `Time.minutes(10)`\n\n### Output Format\nUse `Tuple2<Long, Long>` which prints as `(jobId,count)` by default.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107,"cache_read_input_tokens":48740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":107,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtEhLArbDwBA1wwYMW3z","type":"assistant","uuid":"badef1fd-9b34-4bc2-9321-acf58a707bb1","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:30:16.307Z"}
{"parentUuid":"badef1fd-9b34-4bc2-9321-acf58a707bb1","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"260b5336-3a47-4997-b0ce-d48901003928","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-fluttering-newell","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_011otoDdUE99ndCXW3HaNmqU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01SQSaysymtuyTzs3xWa96pw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-data-types-pattern.md","content":"# Flink Custom Data Types Pattern\n\n## Overview\nWhen working with Flink, custom data types (POJOs) need to follow certain rules to work with Flink's serialization and type system.\n\n## POJO Requirements for Flink\n1. Class must be public\n2. Must have a public no-arg constructor\n3. All fields must be public OR have getters/setters\n4. Fields must be serializable types\n\n## Example: Event Data Type\n\n```java\npackage clusterdata.datatypes;\n\nimport java.io.Serializable;\n\npublic class TaskEvent implements Serializable {\n    public long timestamp;\n    public String missingInfo;\n    public long jobId;\n    public int taskIndex;\n    public long machineId;\n    public int eventType;\n    public String user;\n    public int schedulingClass;\n    public int priority;\n    public double cpuRequest;\n    public double memoryRequest;\n    public double diskRequest;\n    public int differentMachinesRestriction;\n\n    public TaskEvent() {}\n\n    // Static factory method for parsing CSV lines\n    public static TaskEvent fromString(String line) {\n        TaskEvent event = new TaskEvent();\n        String[] fields = line.split(\",\", -1); // -1 to keep trailing empties\n\n        event.timestamp = fields[0].isEmpty() ? 0 : Long.parseLong(fields[0]);\n        event.missingInfo = fields[1];\n        event.jobId = fields[2].isEmpty() ? 0 : Long.parseLong(fields[2]);\n        // ... parse remaining fields\n\n        return event;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Parsing CSV Notes\n- Use `split(\",\", -1)` to preserve empty trailing fields\n- Always check for empty strings before parsing numbers\n- Use default values (0, \"\") for empty fields\n- Handle `long` for IDs (they can be very large numbers)\n\n## Flink Tuple Types\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.tuple.Tuple2;\n\n// Tuple2 toString() produces: (field0,field1)\nTuple2<Long, Long> result = new Tuple2<>(12345L, 42L);\n// result.toString() -> \"(12345,42)\"\n```\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107,"cache_read_input_tokens":48740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":107,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtEhLArbDwBA1wwYMW3z","type":"assistant","uuid":"61aa8f77-a454-4c4f-938a-33591327b05a","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:30:24.681Z"}
{"parentUuid":"61aa8f77-a454-4c4f-938a-33591327b05a","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"260b5336-3a47-4997-b0ce-d48901003928","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-fluttering-newell","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_011otoDdUE99ndCXW3HaNmqU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01QGVhazvM8w3UnXJRV5AT2C","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-file-io.md","content":"# Flink File I/O\n\n## Reading Gzipped CSV Files\nFlink natively supports reading `.gz` files:\n```java\nDataStream<String> lines = env.readTextFile(\"/path/to/data.csv.gz\");\n```\n\n## Writing Output to File\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.core.fs.FileSystem;\n\n// Write to a single output file\nresult.writeAsText(\"/path/to/output\", FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE)\n      .setParallelism(1);  // Important: single file output\n```\n\nThe `.setParallelism(1)` ensures output goes to a single file rather than being split across parallel subtasks.\n\n## Output Format\n- `Tuple2<Long, Long>` auto-formats as `(first,second)`\n- Each element becomes one line in the output file\n- Example output line: `(6252007148,15)`\n\n## Important Notes\n- `writeAsText` is a legacy API but works in Flink 1.18\n- For streaming jobs, use `OVERWRITE` write mode\n- Set parallelism to 1 on the sink for single-file output\n- Flink may create the output as a directory with part files; using parallelism 1 avoids this\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107,"cache_read_input_tokens":48740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":107,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtEhLArbDwBA1wwYMW3z","type":"assistant","uuid":"6f815060-fc89-48ff-9a38-5922b97e4991","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:30:30.986Z"}
{"parentUuid":"252c618e-6fe0-4297-bc45-60c6e8e8824b","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"260b5336-3a47-4997-b0ce-d48901003928","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-fluttering-newell","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Xyv2YDbchDqpod4MGQoqXT","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-streaming-api.md"}]},"uuid":"9138c8fa-38cc-43db-8e80-1fbd27780eab","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:30:31.367Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-streaming-api.md","content":"# Apache Flink Streaming API (1.18.x)\n\n## Overview\nApache Flink is a distributed stream processing framework. This skill covers the DataStream API for building streaming jobs.\n\n## Setup\n- Flink 1.18.0 with Java 11\n- Dependencies: `flink-streaming-java`, `flink-java`, `flink-clients`\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### StreamExecutionEnvironment\n```java\nStreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();\n```\n\n### Reading from files (including gzipped)\n```java\n// Flink can read .gz files natively\nDataStream<String> lines = env.readTextFile(\"/path/to/file.csv.gz\");\n```\n\n### DataStream Transformations\n```java\n// Map: transform each element\nDataStream<MyType> mapped = lines.map(line -> parse(line));\n\n// Filter\nDataStream<MyType> filtered = mapped.filter(e -> e.type == 0);\n\n// KeyBy: partition by key for grouped processing\nKeyedStream<MyType, Long> keyed = filtered.keyBy(e -> e.jobId);\n\n// Reduce: aggregate elements per key\nDataStream<MyType> reduced = keyed.reduce((a, b) -> combine(a, b));\n```\n\n### Window Operations\n```java\n// Event time session windows with gap\nkeyed\n  .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n  .process(new ProcessWindowFunction<>() {\n      @Override\n      public void process(Long key, Context ctx,\n              Iterable<TaskEvent> elements, Collector<Tuple2<Long,Long>> out) {\n          long count = 0;\n          for (TaskEvent e : elements) count++;\n          out.collect(new Tuple2<>(key, count));\n      }\n  });\n```\n\n### Event Time & Watermarks\n```java\n// Assign timestamps and watermarks for event-time processing\nDataStream<MyEvent> withTimestamps = stream\n    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n        WatermarkStrategy.<MyEvent>forMonotonousTimestamps()\n            .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.timestamp / 1000) // convert micros to millis\n    );\n```\n\n### Writing Output\n```java\n// Write to text file\nresult.writeAsText(\"/path/to/output\", FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE)\n      .setParallelism(1);\n```\n\n### Connecting Streams\n```java\n// Connect two streams for co-processing\nDataStream<A> streamA = ...;\nDataStream<B> streamB = ...;\nConnectedStreams<A, B> connected = streamA.connect(streamB);\nDataStream<Result> result = connected.keyBy(a -> a.key, b -> b.key)\n    .process(new CoProcessFunction<>() { ... });\n```\n\n### Tuple Types\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.tuple.Tuple2;\nTuple2<Long, Long> t = new Tuple2<>(jobId, count);\n// Output format: (jobId,count)\n```\n\n## Event Time Processing Notes\n- Flink event time is in **milliseconds**\n- Google cluster data timestamps are in **microseconds**\n- Must convert: `eventTimeMicros / 1000` for Flink timestamps\n- Use `WatermarkStrategy.forMonotonousTimestamps()` when data is sorted by time\n- Use `WatermarkStrategy.forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration)` for out-of-order data\n\n## Session Windows\nSession windows group elements that arrive within a specified gap of each other.\n- `EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10))` creates sessions with 10-minute gap\n- Elements within 10 minutes of each other are in the same session\n- Session closes when no new elements arrive for 10 minutes\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"252c618e-6fe0-4297-bc45-60c6e8e8824b"}
{"parentUuid":"bf60f992-a50b-42ec-b198-1872f171077e","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"260b5336-3a47-4997-b0ce-d48901003928","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-fluttering-newell","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01WB1ZqdcqEhPhZK8WbaHhHw","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/google-cluster-data-schema.md"}]},"uuid":"fa62be58-8a35-4f04-98c7-e45cd811965b","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:30:31.391Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/google-cluster-data-schema.md","content":"# Google Cluster Data 2011-2 Schema\n\n## Overview\nThe Google cluster-usage traces dataset (clusterdata-2011-2) represents 29 days of Borg cell information from May 2011. All timestamps are in **microseconds**.\n\n## Task Events Table\nCSV with 13 fields (0-indexed):\n\n| Index | Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | timestamp | long | Event time in microseconds |\n| 1 | missing_info | string | Info about missing data (can be empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | task_index | int | Task index within the job |\n| 4 | machine_id | long | Machine the task runs on (can be empty) |\n| 5 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 6 | user | string | Hashed user name |\n| 7 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class (0-3) |\n| 8 | priority | int | Priority level (0-11) |\n| 9 | cpu_request | double | CPU resource request |\n| 10 | memory_request | double | Memory resource request |\n| 11 | disk_request | double | Disk resource request |\n| 12 | different_machines_restriction | int | Machine constraint |\n\n## Job Events Table\nCSV with 8 fields (0-indexed):\n\n| Index | Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | timestamp | long | Event time in microseconds |\n| 1 | missing_info | string | Info about missing data (can be empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 4 | user | string | Hashed user name |\n| 5 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class |\n| 6 | job_name | string | Hashed job name |\n| 7 | logical_job_name | string | Hashed logical job name |\n\n## Event Types (shared for both job and task events)\n| Value | Name | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | SUBMIT | Job/task submitted |\n| 1 | SCHEDULE | Job/task scheduled on machine |\n| 2 | EVICT | Task evicted from machine |\n| 3 | FAIL | Task/job failed |\n| 4 | FINISH | Task/job finished normally |\n| 5 | KILL | Task/job killed |\n| 6 | LOST | Task lost (communication failure) |\n| 7 | UPDATE_PENDING | Task resource request updated while pending |\n| 8 | UPDATE_RUNNING | Task resource request updated while running |\n\n## Notes\n- Fields can be empty (e.g., machine_id for SUBMIT events)\n- Timestamps start at ~600 seconds (= 600,000,000 microseconds)\n- Data files are gzipped CSV with no header row\n- Job IDs are shared between task_events and job_events tables\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf60f992-a50b-42ec-b198-1872f171077e"}
{"parentUuid":"badef1fd-9b34-4bc2-9321-acf58a707bb1","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"260b5336-3a47-4997-b0ce-d48901003928","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-fluttering-newell","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01D9dcrKik5qFydmUr9Zy8Se","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-session-window-pattern.md"}]},"uuid":"912c44dd-a41d-4d7a-a9f7-3da3ff985814","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:30:31.407Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-session-window-pattern.md","content":"# Flink Session Window Pattern for Stage Detection\n\n## Problem Pattern\nIdentify \"stages\" of activity for a keyed entity based on event-time gaps. A stage ends when there's a period of inactivity exceeding a threshold.\n\n## Solution: Event-Time Session Windows\n\n### Approach\n1. Parse input events, extract timestamp and key\n2. Assign event-time timestamps and watermarks\n3. Filter to relevant events (e.g., SUBMIT events only)\n4. Key by the grouping field (e.g., job_id)\n5. Apply session window with the inactivity gap\n6. Count elements per window to get stage sizes\n7. Take the maximum stage size per key\n\n### Implementation Pattern\n\n```java\n// Step 1-2: Parse and assign timestamps\nDataStream<TaskEvent> taskEvents = env.readTextFile(inputPath)\n    .map(line -> TaskEvent.parse(line))\n    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n        WatermarkStrategy.<TaskEvent>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ZERO)\n            .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.timestamp / 1000)\n    );\n\n// Step 3-4: Filter SUBMIT events and key by job\nDataStream<TaskEvent> submits = taskEvents.filter(e -> e.eventType == 0);\nKeyedStream<TaskEvent, Long> keyed = submits.keyBy(e -> e.jobId);\n\n// Step 5-6: Session window + count\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> stageCounts = keyed\n    .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .apply(new WindowFunction<TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Long>, Long, TimeWindow>() {\n        @Override\n        public void apply(Long jobId, TimeWindow window,\n                Iterable<TaskEvent> input, Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) {\n            long count = 0;\n            for (TaskEvent e : input) count++;\n            out.collect(new Tuple2<>(jobId, count));\n        }\n    });\n\n// Step 7: Find max stage per job\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> maxStagePerJob = stageCounts\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0)\n    .reduce((a, b) -> a.f1 >= b.f1 ? a : b);\n```\n\n### Key Considerations\n- **Timestamp conversion**: Google cluster data uses microseconds, Flink uses milliseconds\n- **Watermark strategy**: Use monotonous timestamps if data is sorted, bounded out-of-orderness otherwise\n- **Parallelism**: Set output sink to parallelism 1 to get single output file\n- **Session gap**: 10 minutes = `Time.minutes(10)`\n\n### Output Format\nUse `Tuple2<Long, Long>` which prints as `(jobId,count)` by default.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"badef1fd-9b34-4bc2-9321-acf58a707bb1"}
